  "limits": [
    "SystemOne requires SDK 1.7 admission and execution; legacy module actions cannot bypass it, and Jev never receives chat authority.",
    "Provider API Chat/Responses/Messages preserve their native response bytes. The Go-plan module wire accepts canonical Chat; the host's generic adapters translate other clients. The base candidate requires the separately recorded generic completion overlay; final merged-host replay remains pending.",
    "Provider API streaming requests and SSE responses require an explicit canonical protocol terminal before a completed SDK receipt. EOF-only, malformed events and malformed tails stay uncertain without altering forwarded bytes; opaque non-streaming JSON forwarding remains unchanged.",
    "The authorized generic host fix drains at most MaxChunkBytes trailing body bytes for at most two seconds before canceling and joining. Caller cancellation, late errors, excessive tails and missing receipts retain uncertainty and no-replay. The immutable candidate packet remains unchanged; source overlay identity is distinct from its tree and any future commit.",
    "Only a complete native pause_turn body permits an identical-body continuation, at most five. Truncation, late errors, exhausted pauses and refused continuations stay uncertain without a successful terminal or retry.",
    "Inclusive native input stays inclusive in Chat output; the completed SDK receipt subtracts cache reads and writes once to match the host ledger. Inconsistent late cache splits cannot authorize continuation or success.",
    "Unsupported native controls are refused: direct non-Chat module protocols, tool-result images, non-auto tool_choice, parallel_tool_calls=false, disabled reasoning without recovered thinking support, response_format and stream options other than include_usage=true.",
    "Google Chat/native function schemas inline supported nested local references with annotations; cyclic or excessive expansion is explicitly refused. Direct root definitions, unresolved/external references and non-schema data are preserved.",
    "No live vendor requests, real browser approval, real CLI credential import or actual CommandCode CLI continuation is acceptance evidence.",
    "Explicit CommandCode profile config uses host-checked file snapshots and native Library locations; native history is not recovered or advertised.",
    "API 1.9 agent snapshots supply effective maxOutput/efforts/defaultEffort; canonical none uses vendor off, only CommandCode-supported levels are emitted, unknown limits are not invented and user overrides remain authoritative.",
    "API 1.9 decisionModels is validated separately; no recovered CommandCode decision-configuration schema authorizes writing it into vendor settings or conversational models.",
    "Canceling a host authentication receipt blocks account installation; pending loopback callbacks additionally expire after ten minutes or component disposal."
  ]
